{"id":"0624e99112a7488f","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-thm-projective-determinacy.md","title":"Projective Determinacy","display":"thm-projective-determinacy — Projective Determinacy","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-projective-determinacy","aliases":["58-thm-projective-determinacy","Projective Determinacy","PD"],"display":"thm-projective-determinacy — Projective Determinacy","depends_on":["[[58-thm-determinacy]]","[[58-df-projective-hierarchy]]","[[58-df-woodin]]","[[58-df-measurable-cardinal]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-supremum]]","[[../batch18/58-df-determinacy.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-projective-determinacy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-projective-determinacy</span><span>Projective Determinacy</span><span>PD</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-projective-determinacy — Projective Determinacy"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"db916f1fec757e0b\" href=\"?note=db916f1fec757e0b\" title=\"58-thm-determinacy\">58-thm-determinacy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d4ac523055965e48\" href=\"?note=d4ac523055965e48\" title=\"58-df-projective-hierarchy\">58-df-projective-hierarchy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"da3159c0c219916e\" href=\"?note=da3159c0c219916e\" title=\"58-df-woodin\">58-df-woodin</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b4fb7c1808c84d14\" href=\"?note=b4fb7c1808c84d14\" title=\"58-df-measurable-cardinal\">58-df-measurable-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"da76334bd8496c66\" href=\"?note=da76334bd8496c66\" title=\"58-df-supremum\">58-df-supremum</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"4cc4baec9297fd1e\" href=\"?note=4cc4baec9297fd1e\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-determinacy.md\">../batch18/58-df-determinacy.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_n(\\omega^\\omega),\\Pi^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\">\\(\\Sigma^1_n(\\omega^\\omega),\\Pi^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\\)</span> (projective pointclasses)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Det}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Det}_S\\)</span> (determinacy predicate)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\\)</span> (infinitely many Woodin cardinals with a measurable cardinal above them)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> (measurable-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b4fb7c1808c84d14\" href=\"?note=b4fb7c1808c84d14\" title=\"58-df-measurable-cardinal\">58-df-measurable-cardinal</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Woodin}\">\\(\\mathrm{Woodin}\\)</span> (Woodin-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"da3159c0c219916e\" href=\"?note=da3159c0c219916e\" title=\"58-df-woodin\">58-df-woodin</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sup\">\\(\\sup\\)</span> (set-coded sequence and ordinal supremum)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Det}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Det}_S\\)</span> 使用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"4cc4baec9297fd1e\" href=\"?note=4cc4baec9297fd1e\" title=\"58-df-determinacy\">58-df-determinacy</a> 的自然数完整树专门化；大基数前提按 Woodin 依赖的类量词元语言解释。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{meta}\">\\(\\mathrm{meta}\\)</span> 为本原子在下式引入、量化绑定或仅作层级/排版标签的记号；其参数次序与适用域由相应公式固定，不作为额外的未声明外部对象。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pd\\text{-}large\\text{-}cardinal\\text{-}hypothesis} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\lambda,s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\omega,\\lambda)\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(s(n)&lt;s(n+1)\\land\\mathrm{Woodin}(s(n)))\\land\n\\sup(\\operatorname{ran}(s))&lt;\\lambda\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pd\\text{-}large\\text{-}cardinal\\text{-}hypothesis} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\lambda,s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\omega,\\lambda)\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(s(n)&lt;s(n+1)\\land\\mathrm{Woodin}(s(n)))\\land\n\\sup(\\operatorname{ran}(s))&lt;\\lambda\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy} \\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}} \\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\\to\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall A\\in\\Sigma^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\\cup\\Pi^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\\;\\mathrm{Det}_S(A)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy} \\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}} \\mathrm{PDLargeCardinalHyp}_S\\to\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall A\\in\\Sigma^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\\cup\\Pi^1_n(\\omega^\\omega)\\;\\mathrm{Det}_S(A)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Woodin: revolutionized connection between determinacy and large cardinals.</li>\n<li>Martin–Steel: infinitely many Woodin cardinals with a measurable cardinal above them suffice for projective determinacy.</li>\n<li>The Woodin sequence is a set-coded function; no sequence-valued quantifier is left at the meta level.</li>\n<li>PD is &quot;natural&quot; axiom: captures regularity of reals without full AD.</li>\n<li>Under PD, projective sets are measurable, have the Baire property, and satisfy PSP.</li>\n<li>PD also yields the standard projective ordinal analysis via the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta^1_n\">\\(\\delta^1_n\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Applications: descriptive set theory, inner model theory.</li>\n<li>AD<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"^{\\mathbb{R}}\">\\(^{\\mathbb{R}}\\)</span>: stronger determinacy axiom (all games on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\">\\(\\mathbb{R}\\)</span>).</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-thm-determinacy","status":"resolved","id":"db916f1fec757e0b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-thm-determinacy]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projective-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"d4ac523055965e48","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-projective-hierarchy]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-woodin","status":"resolved","id":"da3159c0c219916e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-woodin]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"b4fb7c1808c84d14","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"5